# IAOS APP SITE — environment variables
#
# Netlify site: iaos-app  →  app.investorautomationos.com  (base directory: app)
#
# This file documents NAMES AND PURPOSES ONLY. It never carries a value, and it
# never carries a placeholder shaped like a value. Copy it to app/.env and fill
# it in locally; app/.env is gitignored.
#
# Every variable below is read by code that app/netlify.toml actually deploys.
# Variables belonging to other consumers live elsewhere on purpose:
#   - the marketing site and local developer tooling  →  ../.env.example
#   - server/                                          →  documented nowhere yet;
#     nothing in either netlify.toml deploys or executes it.
#
# GHL_API_TOKEN IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. It was removed from this surface in
# Gate 4B-1. No code under app/ reads it any more, and listing it here would
# re-document the credential fallback that commit exists to eliminate.


# --- Location selector (PB-D51) ------------------------------------------
# Which GoHighLevel location every identifier resolves to. Accepts exactly
# "production" or "test". There is no default: getConfig throws on an empty,
# missing, or unrecognized value rather than guessing.

# Read by the Netlify functions at module scope — including
# iaos-runtime-config, which is what the browser now fetches at boot. This is
# the ONLY selector on this site.
IAOS_ENV=

# VITE_IAOS_ENV IS GONE as of Gate 4B-5. The frontend no longer receives a
# build-time selector: main.tsx fetches iaos-runtime-config, validates it, and
# only then imports the application. The built artifact is therefore identical
# across environments and the environment is decided at request time.
# Do not reintroduce it — doing so would restore build-time coupling that the
# identifier and configuration gates exist to prevent.


# --- Credentials ----------------------------------------------------------

# The GoHighLevel private integration token. REQUIRED by all eleven functions
# on this site. There is no fallback: a missing value is refused before any
# outbound request rather than substituted from a second variable.
GHL_PRIVATE_API_KEY=

# Shared secret for the inbound disposition webhook (ghl-disposition). GHL
# sends it as X-IAOS-Secret; the function compares it in constant time and
# refuses the request when it does not match.
IAOS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Resend API key. Sends the weekly mailer digest (mailer-digest, ghl-mailers).
RESEND_API_KEY=


# --- Board #14 outbound voice foundation (TEST only) ---------------------
# Disabled unless IAOS_ENV=test AND IAOS_VOICE_ENABLED is exactly "true".
# INV-90 provisions no account, credential, number, charge, or live call.
IAOS_VOICE_ENABLED=

# Google Identity Services audience and the explicit Brad-only email allowlist.
# The server verifies the Google ID token, then issues a 15-minute IAOS JWT.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
IAOS_VOICE_BRAD_EMAILS=
IAOS_VOICE_SESSION_SECRET=

# Twilio server credentials. API key values mint outbound-only browser tokens;
# the auth token verifies Twilio webhook signatures. None is browser-exposed.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_API_KEY_SID=
TWILIO_API_KEY_SECRET=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_TWIML_APP_SID=

# Must eventually be the Brad-controlled GHL business number verified by
# Twilio, never a newly purchased or ported number under INV-90.
TWILIO_OUTBOUND_CALLER_ID=

# Exact public TEST origin used to build and validate signed callback URLs.
IAOS_VOICE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
